  },
  {
    "q": "What's the difference between \"known unknowns\" and \"unknown unknowns\"?",
    "a": "Known unknowns are failures you've seen before and can write a monitoring rule for a full disk, a slow dependency. Unknown unknowns are failures nobody predicted a rare combination of service, region, and load that only observability's exploratory approach can uncover."
